<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liège Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1789–1791</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liège Revolution began in August 1789, when citizens drove out Prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Hoensbroeck, installed new magistrates and later proclaimed a republic. It was suppressed by Austrian troops in January 1791, but the French revolutionary armies returned in 1792 and 1794, and the principality was annexed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1795.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liege-revolution.jpg" alt="Liège Revolution" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liege-ruine-stlambert-Chevron-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
